      {
        "id": 14697,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-04T07:11:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So, I was trying to unlock DW Nightmist, and I had things perfectly set up. &nbsp;Nightmist had Master of Magic in play, Oblivion* in hand, and Argent Adept has two Vernal Sonatas ready to put two 4s on top of my deck. &nbsp;But there is a slight problem. &nbsp;Actually, two slight problems. &nbsp;The first is that I only have one 4 in the trash (having just used a Mist Fueled Recovery on AA's turn in order to come back up from 9 life), and there's an Ethereal Bonds in play ready to paralyze Nightmist. &nbsp;So, what do I do? &nbsp;I could just discard a 4 to Mistbound, but that wouldn't deal with the Bonds. &nbsp;I have a Planar Banishment, but that isn't a 4.</p><p>But! &nbsp;I actually have two Oblivions, and one of them is a 4. &nbsp;So my plan is this: &nbsp;Play Oblivion, kill the Bonds, and then on the next turn Vernal Sonata twice (using Alacritous Subdominant) to put the two 4s on top of the deck, and then Oblivion. &nbsp;Sounds like a plan! &nbsp;So I play Oblivion, and... flip two 4s accidentally, and unlock the variant a turn earlier than I had planned. &nbsp;Whoops.</p><p><span>I then proceeded to crush Voss as he so rightly deserved.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>*Suddenly, spelling \"Oblivion\" normally is really difficult. &nbsp;I'm really looking forward to defeating OblivAeon using Oblivion.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:46:51.702Z",
